            "review_title": "Review at Nam Chau Seafood Restaurant",
            "review_text": "YY_Xie\nSingapore, Singapore654 contributions\n0\nFresh seafood\nAug 2026 • Solo\nI wanted to go to Mộc Quán Seafood, but the wait was too long, and last order for grilled items would have been over by the time I got a table. So I went to Nam Chau, which was a stone's throw away, for my seafood fix. By contrast, the place was empty, but it had decent reviews, so I gave it a try. I ordered the Japanese ocean scallop grilled with scallion and peanut sauce, and spiny lobster cooked in 2 styles: fried garlic & garlic butter. The seafood was fresh, but I found the scallops kinda small. A large spiny lobster (market price) was approximately 25% cheaper than in Singapore, so I guess the price was somewhat reasonable. I very much preferred the fried garlic to garlic butter. Service was brisk & attentive. Like other seafood restaurants in the area, the wait staff would deshell the lobster for customers as part of standard service. Cards accepted here.\nRead more\nWritten August 15, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
